{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Neurology\n\nDomain hub: localisation, examination and diagnostic reasoning, with the main neurological disorder categories and their mechanisms.\n\n[[Neurology Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-27; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 2190,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[History and localisation]]**\n*method* - 7 sources\n\nLocalisation as clinical reasoning: using history, examination and anatomy together to infer where a problem is.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neurological examination]]**\n*method* - 5 sources\n\nThe neurological examination as a localisation method: its domains, its reasoning frame and the limits of a normal result.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 598,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Differential reasoning in neurology]]**\n*framework* - 9 sources\n\nHow neurological differentials are constructed: mechanism, timing, distribution and the tests that change probabilities.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 836,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[EEG and other diagnostics]]**\n*method* - 6 sources\n\nWhat EEG, evoked potentials, cerebrospinal fluid studies and nerve conduction tests contribute, and what each cannot settle.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1074,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Method",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1006
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[MRI versus EEG]]**\n*method* - 6 sources\n\nMRI, fMRI and EEG compared on signal, temporal and spatial resolution, and the inference each supports.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Structural versus functional measures]]**\n*framework* - 4 sources\n\nStructure and function as different levels of measurement, why group differences are not diagnoses, and the confounds that complicate clinical imaging findings.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 598,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Interpreting group brain differences]]**\n*method* - 6 sources\n\nWhat group-average imaging findings establish, how medication and course confound them, and why they do not become individual tests.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 860,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Measurement",
			"x": 460,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 792
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Seizures and epilepsy]]**\n*condition* - 8 sources\n\nSeizure types, the definition of epilepsy, evaluation logic and the principles behind antiseizure treatment.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Cerebrovascular disease]]**\n*condition* - 4 sources\n\nStroke and related vascular disease: mechanisms, risk factors, urgency and the logic of vascular territory deficits.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 598,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Demyelination and multiple sclerosis]]**\n*condition* - 6 sources\n\nImmune-mediated demyelination, its clinical courses, the diagnostic logic, and what myelin loss does to signalling.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 836,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Movement disorders]]**\n*condition* - 5 sources\n\nTremor, chorea, dystonia, rigidity and bradykinesia: how movement disorders are distinguished and mapped onto circuits.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 1074,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neurodegeneration and cognitive syndromes]]**\n*condition* - 6 sources\n\nProgressive neurodegeneration, the dementia syndrome, and the distinction between clinical and pathological diagnosis.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 1312,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Peripheral neuropathy and neuromuscular disease]]**\n*condition* - 5 sources\n\nDisorders of peripheral nerves and the neuromuscular junction: causes, patterns and the logic of length-dependent deficits.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 1574,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Headache and pain]]**\n*condition* - 3 sources\n\nPrimary headache disorders, nociceptive mechanisms, and the distinction between pain as a symptom and pain as a condition.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 1836,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Sleep disorders]]**\n*condition* - 6 sources\n\nInsomnia, sleep-related breathing problems, circadian rhythm disorders and parasomnias, and how sleep is assessed.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 2074,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_8",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Traumatic brain injury]]**\n*condition* - 6 sources\n\nBrain injury from external force: how severity is graded, why symptoms can persist after a mild injury, and how TBI overlaps with PTSD and ADHD in ways that complicate attribution.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_9",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Functional neurological disorder]]**\n*condition* - 4 sources\n\nGenuine neurological symptoms arising from altered brain function rather than structural damage: the positive-sign diagnosis, its subtypes, mechanism research, links with trauma and dissociation, and the treatment evidence.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 646,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_10",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Tic disorders and Tourette syndrome]]**\n*condition* - 5 sources\n\nChildhood-onset motor and vocal tics: features, course, the high rates of co-occurring ADHD and OCD, and the classes of treatment option, from education and watchful waiting to behavioural therapy, medication and deep brain stimulation.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 956,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#F59E3B"
		},
		{
			"id": "g2",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Conditions",
			"x": 920,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 810,
			"height": 1982
		},
		{
